// Certificate of appreciation issued to a case's backers when the case is marked
// Closed (JUS: case-closing workflow).
//
// One row per (case, backer). A "backer" is anyone with a succeeded donation to
// the case — including guests, who have no account (`donorId` null) and are
// identified by `donorEmail`. Closing a case is not a refund: the certificate is
// the acknowledgement donors receive, and the copy everywhere says so.
//
// Generation is idempotent. `dedupeKey` is unique per (case, backer), so
// re-running the close fan-out — a retried action, a re-close — inserts nothing
// new. `serial` and `accessToken` are minted once, at insert.
//
// Access. `accessToken` is an unguessable capability: the certificate page is a
// public route keyed by it, so a guest with no account still reaches their
// certificate from the emailed link. Account backers reach the same page from
// their donations screen and an in-app notification.
//
// Email is claimed exactly once via `emailedAt` under a status-conditional
// update — the same reserve-then-send discipline the notification and donation
// emails use — so a redelivery or re-close never double-sends. The reservation
// lives here rather than on a Notification row because guest backers have no
// account and so no notification to reserve against.
model Certificate {
  id     String @id @default(cuid())
  case   Case   @relation(fields: [caseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  caseId String

  // The backer's account, when they had one. Null for guest donations — see the
  // Donation model. `donorEmail` is always the identity we can reach them at.
  donorId    String?
  donorEmail String?


  // Snapshots taken at issue time, so the certificate stays truthful even if the
  // case is later edited or the donor renames their account.
  recipientName String
  caseTitle     String
  // The backer's total succeeded contribution to this case, in cents. Aggregated
  // across every gift they made — one certificate acknowledges the person, not
  // the transaction.
  amountCents   Int

  // Human-facing certificate number shown on the certificate (e.g. JU-2K4F9).
  serial String @unique
  // Unguessable capability that gates the public certificate page.
  accessToken String @unique

  // One (case, backer) = one row; unique so a re-close skips duplicates.
  dedupeKey String @unique

  issuedAt  DateTime  @default(now())
  createdAt DateTime  @default(now())
  // Stamped when the "your certificate is ready" email is claimed for sending.
  emailedAt DateTime?

  @@index([caseId])
  @@index([donorId])
  @@map("certificate")
}
